## 3.6. Summary of Results  
Taken together, the most no from our data is that FD is exceptionally effective in preserving physical coloration and nutritional and bioactive compositions, although it results in a remarkable decrease in the abundances of aroma components. The beverage derived from FD-LSs also exhibited the highest levels of the vast majority of available active ingredients and antioxidant activities. However, it is crucial to acknowledge that FD a fairly time-consuming and costly drying method, primarily due to the operation of vacuum and refrigeration systems, which lead to slow drying rates and higher energy consumption. Consequently, the price of commercially available FD-LSs is often several times higher than that of hot-dried LSs. On the other hand, among the tested thermal drying processes, HPD-LSs revealed relatively appealing color, high levels of both natural and available bioactive compounds  
), and aroma compounds, as well as enhanced available amounts of active compounds and antioxidant activities.
